# Server architecture

Pipeline (do not reorder):

`json → cors → cookieParser → health/docs → routers → notFound → errorHandler`

New endpoint:

1. Zod in `server/packages/api-contract`
2. Route: `authMiddleware`? + `validate(schema)` + `asyncHandler`
3. Controller: call service, return `{ success: true, message, data }`
4. Service: throw `AppError(status, code, message, details?)` — never `res`
5. Repository: Drizzle only — never Express, never user-facing strings

```ts
// BAD — Drizzle in controller
const rows = await db.select().from(users);

// GOOD
const user = await userRepository.findById(id);
```

```ts
// BAD — catch 500 in every handler
} catch (e) { res.status(500).json({ message: "Internal server error" }); }

// GOOD
export const get = asyncHandler(async (req, res) => { ... });
```

Error body always: `{ success: false, code, message, details: [] }`.

Ownership: `row.userId === req.auth.userId` or `403 FORBIDDEN`.

Lists: cursor + `API_PAGE_LIMIT` (50), newest first.

Auth: Bearer then cookie. bcrypt 12. Strip `password`. Generic sign-in errors.

Payment status transitions live only in `services/paymentStatus.ts`. Create attempt + transaction in one DB transaction. Idempotency `(userId, idempotencyKey)`.
